<title>UK: RR says Continental order worth over $650 mln.</title>
<headline>RR says Continental order worth over $650 mln.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rolls-Royce Plc said on Tuesday that a previously announced Continental Express order for 25 EMB-145 aircraft and an option to buy 175 more was worth over $650 million to its U.S.-based engine making Allison unit.  </p>
<p>Allison's AE 3007, rated at 7600 pounds thrust, powers the EMB-145 aircraft.</p>
<p>&quot;This is the largest single commercial order for our new AE 3007 turbofan,&quot; said Allison Engine Company's vice president of large commercial engines, A S Novick, in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
